As you can see, the code is seeing the RA's hop_limit, but that is not being sent in the IP header.

Which code change is meant to cause the hop_limit from the RA to be written to the IP header on the next response?

I have verified a patch for this.  I added the following function to `src/network/networkd-ndisc.c`

```
static int ndisc_router_process_hop_limit(Link *link, sd_ndisc_router *rt) {
        uint8_t hop_limit;
        int r;

        assert(link);
        assert(link->network);
        assert(rt);

        if (!link->network->ipv6_accept_ra_use_retransmission_time)
                return 0;

        r = sd_ndisc_router_get_hop_limit(rt, &hop_limit);
        if (r < 0) {
                log_link_debug_errno(link, r, "Failed to get hop_limit from RA, ignoring: %m");
                return 0;
        }

        if (hop_limit == 0 || hop_limit > UINT8_MAX)
                return 0;

        /* Set the hop_limit for this interface. */
        r = sysctl_write_ip_property_uint32(AF_INET6, link->ifname, "hop_limit", (uint32_t) hop_limit);
        if (r < 0)
                log_link_warning_errno(
                        link, r, "Failed to apply hop_limit (%d), ignoring: %m", hop_limit);

        return 0;
}
```
I call it from `ndisc_router_handler()`:

```
        r = ndisc_router_process_hop_limit(link, rt);
        if (r < 0)
                return r;
```

After retesting with the conformance test suite, the test now passes.

I'd be grateful if you can add this patch to #31173, which would save me from creating a PR.
